{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F56AZeroSizedAxisPanics",
    "description": "F56. An `interval` index set whose size is 0 makes evaluation PANIC instead of producing an empty relation. `esm validate` accepts this document; `esm test` aborts -- with `col_major_to_arrayd shape mismatch: shape [0] (product 0) vs 1 elements` at esm 0.2.0, and at 0.3.1 one stage later, naming the output rows, with `attempt to calculate the remainder with a divisor of zero` -- a message addressed to the implementor rather than to the author.\n\nThe document is the whole repro: one metaparameter at its default of 0, one axis sized by it, one variable over that axis, and a `faq` that would sum an empty range -- whose answer is the semiring's identity over no terms, which for sum_product is a relation of length 0. THE ASSERTION BELOW IS UNREACHABLE and deliberately so: the axis has no cell 1, so if this document ever stops panicking it will fail on the assertion instead, which is the second half of the fix and a distinguishable message.\n\nWHERE IT BIT. `onroad/model.esm` is data-open: it declares 51 metaparameters, every one of them discovered from a `data_source` `extent` that only a mounting catalogue supplies, so evaluating it ALONE sizes every axis at 0. `esm validate` refuses it cleanly, naming the sources it does not declare. `esm test` panics. That is why run-tests.sh excludes `onroad/` from its test targets and checks the model through its catalogues instead -- an exclusion that reads like tidiness and is not.\n\nWHAT IS NOT THE DEFECT: a zero-length axis used only as a `faq` RANGE is fine. `runspecs/expand-day.esm` ingests a `runspecchainedto` of 0 rows -- nothing in that run is chained -- and evaluates correctly, because no emitted variable is shaped over that axis. The panic needs a relation MATERIALIZED at length 0.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["finding", "shape", "panic"]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_empty": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "0, which is what every `extent`-discovered metaparameter in a data-open document is worth when the document is evaluated alone."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "empty_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": "n_empty" }
  },
  "models": {
    "F56AZeroSizedAxisPanics": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },
      "variables": {
        "empty_value": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": ["empty_rows"],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "A relation over an axis of length 0. It should be an empty relation."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "empty_value",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": ["e"],
            "ranges": { "e": { "from": "empty_rows" } },
            "expr": 1.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "an_axis_of_length_zero_is_an_empty_relation_and_not_a_panic",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "empty_value",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 1,
              "coords": { "empty_rows": 1 }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
